1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,240
“Just one more trade…

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,254
I'll win it all back.”

3
00:00:04,254 --> 00:00:06,516
Rohit has already
lost forty thousand.

4
00:00:06,516 --> 00:00:09,081
Meera: “Where did
the FD money go?”

5
00:00:09,081 --> 00:00:11,783
His answer… “a friend's
emergency.”

6
00:00:11,783 --> 00:00:14,701
The Rigveda's gambler
knew this “one more” too.

7
00:00:14,701 --> 00:00:18,671
“My wife never fought with me… yet
for one more die…

8
00:00:18,671 --> 00:00:20,059
I pushed her away.”

9
00:00:20,089 --> 00:00:21,379
This is called…

10
00:00:21,379 --> 00:00:22,659
loss chasing.

11
00:00:22,659 --> 00:00:23,749
A loss…

12
00:00:23,749 --> 00:00:25,379
then “one more”…

13
00:00:25,379 --> 00:00:27,795
a bigger loss… then hiding it.

14
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:32,515
SEBI: 93% of F&O
traders lost money…

15
00:00:32,515 --> 00:00:35,168
three in four kept on trading.

16
00:00:35,168 --> 00:00:41,695
akṣair mā dīvyaḥ kṛṣim it kṛṣasva…
vitte ramasva bahu manyamānaḥ

17
00:00:41,695 --> 00:00:43,255
“Don't play with dice…

18
00:00:43,255 --> 00:00:44,725
plough your own field…

19
00:00:44,725 --> 00:00:46,693
delight in what you have.”

20
00:00:46,693 --> 00:00:49,356
The hymn says this
advice came from Savitr.

21
00:00:49,356 --> 00:00:50,486
That same night…

22
00:00:50,486 --> 00:00:53,387
app deleted… and the
whole truth to Meera.

23
00:00:53,587 --> 00:00:58,332
Would you tell the truth…
or win it back first?
